592186045417] [17592186262174 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262174 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262174 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262174 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262174 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262174 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186261609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262174 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1f9de2d2-96e1-5828-8e77-3d0b2dfc03ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186260705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262226 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "393f9b0c-bf5c-5bb2-93a1-37868fcb5583" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186260306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262552 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f6b091ac-faa9-5b51-87d6-4183663a28fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262767 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262767 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127401" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262767 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262767 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-2t \\\\ y=5-t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262767 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d2a6473-caac-59fb-8a5c-a6c5ea0abc7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262767 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-2t \\\\ 5-t \\\\ -7+t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ -t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(1,5,-7)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-2,-1,1⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{z-(-7)}{1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{z+7}{1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262774 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262774 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127454" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262774 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262774 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262774 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5ca9c758-73dc-58e9-9495-123d55df1262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262774 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-3)}{7}=\\frac{y-5}{0}=\\frac{z}{2}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{y-5}{0}=\\frac{z}{2},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{y-5}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=5:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3+7t \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y-5}{0}$ part and instead write $y=5$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{z}{2},\\,y=5\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262776 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262776 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262776 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262776 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/16/1647eb5cca32c6fdc99e23507db151a8299b29bfa70ebfbaa941e17fe4638586.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262776 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "137b0f7e-9478-507b-9673-19fabe3f3d94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262776 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,4,5)$ and $Q(7,-1,2).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-1,2⟩-⟨-1,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,-5,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{8}=\\fra